==Strategy==
The R.Ost duo push very hard in this stage. Crowd controlling them is necessary for victory. Money is tight at the start, but with the discount on special units, it shouldn't be difficult to get a stack of strong units going.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
''It is heavily recommended to use Special Cats over other rarities due to how much of a big discount they receive in this stage.''
*[[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]]: While he doesn't have a resistance to Traitless or Relic, his high health and immunity to knockback prevent M. Ost from pushing far into your defense. Riceball is also a Special Cat which allows him to only cost 90¢ and be deployed once every 0.6s which means you can use him as the only meatshield for this stage.
*[[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]]: Thanks to this stage's rule, Ururun can be used similar to a Super Rare with a lot more DPS and range. It's knockback can also be useful to push back the threats in this stage.
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]]: While they take a lot of time to unlock, their guaranteed weaken versus Relics, strong versus Relics, long distance ability and its massive discount it has gotten, it can easily defeats the M. Ost aswell of weakening them.
*[[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]]: Similar to Naala, but with less DPS in exchange for being generally easier to unlock.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]]: His high DPS against Traitless is pretty strong against the R.Ost in this stage. He also get the rules discount for being a special Cat. In short, they remove one of the 2 important threats in this stage.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Mystic Uril]]: His ability to slow relics for a very good uptime and his cost and cooldown being reduced massively thanks to this colosseum rule allow Uril to deal against the M. Ost in this stage greatly. His True form, Esoteric Uril, is a massive boost if you own it.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: He's able to slow all the enemies for a significant amount of time, greatly lowering their pushing power. Slow Up talents recommended.
*[[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Glass Cat]]: They have the ability to knockback ''and'' slow the R.Ost on demand. Its slow is also quite long.
*[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Maize Cat]]: They are tanky against the Relic enemies here. It can slow down the push of M. Ost significantly.
*[[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]]: His Relic/Traitless targeting makes him a perfect pick for this stage, as he is able to easily tank every enemy here.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Chronos]]: Her Freeze can decrease M. Ost's pushing power if protected right,allowing you to focus on killing the R.Ost.
*[[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Doom Phono]]: He has the ability to Slow both every enemy here. Ost. He can make victory very easy by completely denying the R. Osts ability to push back.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: She is able to Freeze the M. Ost, as well as all the other Relic enemies in this stage thanks to her expansive maximum range through Explosion, making the stage much easier.

